Colin wrote:
> I managed to find a couple of bones files and now have a ton of cursed
> stuff that I've moved to a stash.  I'm wondering if there's a way to
> mass uncurse objects; as I understand it, you have to use a potion of
> holy water on each object that you want to uncurse/bless.
>
> Also, what can I do to uncurse stuff when I have found no potions of
> water nor a coaligned altar yet (I'm currently exploring through the
> second level of the mines; there was one non-aligned altar on level 1)?

You asked for spoilers, so spoilers you shall receive.

1. The best way to uncurse things enmasse is to read a blessed scroll
of remove curse while carrying everything you want uncursed.  It'll
uncurse everything in your pack, but it won't touch things inside of
containers.  If you have a blessed magic marker with enough charges in
it and a blank scroll, then this is probably the best solution.  (If
you are confused, then all the items in your pack will be given a
random curse/bless status, which can be a useful means of making holy
water from water if you're cagey enough.)
2. If you zap a pile of items with a wand of cancellation, all the
items in that pile will be uncursed, but there are unpleasant side
effects with many items: scrolls become blank, potions become unmagical
types (often water), weapons and armor become +0 and wands other than
cancellation lose all charges (and in fact will have "-1" charges,
meaning you can't even wrest out a final charge).  Magic equipment and
tools, however, if they don't have magic charges, will usually come out
okay.
3. I'm unsure of the details, but if you pray and have no outstanding
troubles to cure, one of the possible results is having your stuff
uncursed.  Having a high luck or standing on a co-aligned altar may
increase the chances, but it's also possible to have nothing happen, or
to be crowned (which could be viewed as negative in some respects).

Beyond that:
4. Dipping in fountains can sometimes break a curse on a single object
or stack, but some items will be harmed by the water.
5. Dipping in holy water, of course, will move an object towards being
uncursed one step.  (Cursed -> uncursed -> blessed.)  You can dip a
while stack of items in one potion.
6. If the items are water or unholy water, the process of making holy
water on a co-aligned altar naturally undoes the curse, so you don't
have to worry about uncursing them specifically.

